  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "Prior to the commencement of any external works hereby approved, a comprehensive, detailed methodology and schedule of works for all external interventions (including the treatment of the columns, windows, doors, painted render, and portico) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The documentation must be prepared by a qualified conservation architect or a recognised skilled heritage craftsperson. The works shall thereafter be executed strictly in accordance with the approved details.  \r\rReason: To ensure that the specialist craftsmanship required for the external historic fabric is maintained, safeguarding the architectural and historic interest of the Grade II listed building in accordance with Policy 30 of the Sutton Local Plan.",
    "Prior to the commencement of the external repairs, physical sample panels measuring 50cm x 50cm demonstrating the proposed repairs, materials, and finishes to all external surfaces, specifically including the entrance columns, external render, and the tympanum, shall be prepared on-site for inspection. No external repair or rendering works shall take place until these sample panels have been approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority, and the development shall be completed in accordance with the approved samples.  \r\rReason: To ensure a high-quality finish that is visually sympathetic to the historic character of the heritage asset, in accordance with Policies 28 and 30 of the Sutton Local Plan and Guideline G5 of the Carshalton Village CA Character Appraisal.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Safety Statement prepared Redsquare Architects Ltd.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12."
  ],
